course: dictionary
lesson: 13652
title: Words that change meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence around them shows you which one to use. Read the clues before you decide. Here the word is inflame.
explain: «The coach's speech inflamed the crowd, and they started shouting at the referee.» Inflamed means made people angrier or more excited. The clue is that they started shouting at the referee.
explain: «Mia's knee was inflamed, red and hot and sore after her fall.» This time inflamed is about the body. The knee became red, swollen, hot and painful. The clue is the word sore.
explain: Test your meaning in the sentence. Does «made the crowd angrier» make sense? Does «red, hot and sore» fit the knee? The meaning that fits the sentence is the right one.
fact: Inflame means to make something stronger, angrier or more painful.
fact: «Inflame» can mean to make people angrier or more excited.
fact: «An inflamed knee» is red, swollen, hot and painful, often from infection or injury.
fact: «Inflamed» is the past form of inflame, as in «The cut became inflamed».
fact: Old books use inflame to mean set on fire, but this meaning is rare today.
exercise: «The speech inflamed the crowd.» What does inflamed mean here? | *Made them angrier and more excited | Made them fall asleep | Made them feel cold | Made them go home quietly
exercise: «Ben's throat was inflamed, so it hurt to swallow.» What does inflamed mean here? | Cool and wet | Full of music | *Red, swollen and sore | Very tall
exercise: In «The rude comment inflamed the argument», what does inflamed most likely mean? | Ended the argument | Painted the argument | Made the argument quieter | *Made the argument worse
test: «The bee sting made his arm inflamed and swollen.» What does inflamed mean here? | *Red, hot and sore | Cold and dry | Quiet and calm | Fast and happy
test: «News of the lie inflamed tensions between the two towns.» What does inflamed tensions mean? | *Made the feelings between them worse | Brought the towns together | Sent the towns a card | Made the towns cooler
exam: A speech can make a crowd furious. Which is the best meaning of inflame here? | Make people feel cold | *Make people angrier | Make people feel calm | Put people to sleep
